# Line endings for the AIAE-managed agent surface and shell scripts.
#
# `.claude/.aiae-fixtures-manifest` records a SHA-256 for every file the AIAE
# installer (`install-claude-fixtures.sh` in AIAE-replit-llm-aux) owns. The
# installer refuses to upgrade when any of those files differs byte-for-byte,
# so a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewriting their line endings
# would block the next template upgrade. The standard itself is mixed (most files
# LF, a few CRLF), so no single eol policy matches the manifest: `-text` stores
# and restores the installer's bytes exactly. Do not "tidy" this into eol=lf.
#
# Shell scripts are pinned to LF because CRLF breaks them on Linux/Replit
# ("bad interpreter").
#
# Everything else keeps the repository's existing behaviour (no global rule).

.claude/agent_docs/** -text
.claude/rules/** -text
.claude/skills/** -text
.claude/tasks/README.md -text
.claude/.aiae-fixtures-manifest -text
.agents/** -text
CLAUDE.md -text
AGENTS.md text eol=lf
replit.md text eol=lf
AI-DEVELOPMENT-GUIDE.md -text
GDS-WORKFLOW-README.md -text
agent-payload.skills -text
llm-aux.lock text eol=lf
.template-version text eol=lf
.template-phase text eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/lib/*.py text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf
